Why Is Demand Increasing
Medical Device Packaging — Increasing production of medical devices and consumables is creating demand for reliable sterile-barrier packaging materials.
Sterilization Compatibility — Medical kraft paper can be designed for sterilization processes including ethylene oxide, steam, and gamma radiation, making it suitable for diverse healthcare packaging requirements.
Sustainable Packaging — Growing attention to packaging sustainability is encouraging healthcare manufacturers to evaluate paper-based materials alongside performance, sterility, and barrier requirements.

Healthcare Packaging Watch: Sterile-Barrier Performance Drives Adoption
Medical packaging suppliers are balancing mechanical strength, breathability, seal performance, sterilization compatibility, and protection against contamination. Healthcare manufacturers are also evaluating packaging materials based on process efficiency, storage requirements, product visibility, and sustainability considerations. This is creating opportunities for specialized kraft-paper grades and engineered medical packaging structures.

